{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Imglink: three mobile cart-drawer fixes that are all about TAP and
  SCROLL behaviour in #cart. Named for the first; the other two live here
  because overlay-group is at Shopify's hard limit of 25 sections and this is
  the drawer's interaction file.

  ================================================================
  1. TAPPING A CART ITEM'S PICTURE OPENS THAT PRODUCT'S PAGE.

  In the cart drawer each line item draws its thumbnail as

      <li> ... <figure><picture><img ...></picture></figure> ... </li>

  with NO anchor anywhere above the image -- the only link in the row is the
  product TITLE. On a phone that title is a small target sitting beside a big
  photo, and the photo is the thing shoppers actually tap, so tapping it did
  nothing and the row felt broken.

  WHY A DELEGATED LISTENER, NOT AN <a> WRAPPER. Wrapping the figure in an
  anchor would give real link semantics (long-press, open in new tab), but the
  theme replaces the drawer's contents wholesale on every add, remove and
  quantity change, and pg-cart-smooth's morph re-uses the surviving nodes. A
  wrapper would have to be re-applied after every one of those passes, and
  re-parenting nodes underneath the morph is exactly the kind of fight that
  produced the earlier upsell "spazzing". One listener bound once to the
  document, matched with closest(), survives every re-render without touching
  the DOM at all.

  THE CASE IS EXCLUDED, deliberately and by request. The R36S Protective Case
  ships as a free gift with the console, so its line in the cart is an outcome
  of the console purchase rather than something to go shopping for -- sending
  someone to its product page mid-cart is a detour, not a feature. It is matched
  on the product handle rather than on price or a "free" label, so the spare
  case (a real, paid variant of the same product) is excluded with it and a
  future change to the gift's price cannot silently switch the link back on.

  WHAT IT WILL NOT SWALLOW. The handler bails on anything that is already
  interactive -- the title link, the Remove and Undo links, the quantity
  steppers, any button, input or label -- so every existing control keeps its
  own behaviour. It also bails when the shopper is dragging out a text
  selection, and on anything but an unmodified primary click, so long-press and
  middle-click are left alone.

  Mobile only (760px, the same breakpoint the rest of the cart work uses), which
  is where the request came from; desktop rows are wider and the title link is
  an easy target there.
  ================================================================
  2. THE FREE-3rd-ORB CHOOSER OPENED WHERE NOBODY COULD SEE IT

  Reported as "it shows the option to add a 3rd free but when you do it doesn't
  let you select -- the selection drawer doesn't open". The drawer DOES open.
  Measured on a 390x844 phone with two orbs in the cart: tapping Add sets
  is-open on the row and .pg-unlock-pick becomes display:block, 137px tall, with
  its select inside. It is simply invisible.

  The reason is the pinned checkout pane. .sticky-in-panel is
  position:sticky, bottom:-34px, z-index:5 and painted solid white, 291px tall,
  and it sits across the bottom of the drawer. The offer row is in normal flow
  BEHIND it: measured, the row spans y=535..799 while the pane starts at y=553.
  So the moment the panel expands, the whole picker is behind an opaque panel.
  Nothing is broken -- it is covered.

  THE FIRST FIX FOR THIS DID NOT WORK, and the reason is recorded here because it
  is the same fact that explains the freeze below. It scrolled the drawer by the
  overlap -- but this scroller IGNORES scrollTop: assigning it reads back 0
  (measured, twice). So the scroll was a silent no-op on a real device. The check
  that passed it only passed because that particular run had already ended up
  clear for an unrelated reason. A verification that cannot fail is not a
  verification.

  So the row is now RAISED instead of scrolled: while it is open it gets
  position:relative and z-index:6, one above the pane's 5, and paints over it.
  That depends on nothing but stacking order, which cannot silently do nothing.

  The objection to this the first time round was that it puts the picker over the
  CHECKOUT button. It does, and that is the right trade: the alternative is a
  shopper who cannot pick their free orb at all. It is also brief -- only while
  the row is open -- and the select itself opens as a native OS sheet, not as an
  in-page dropdown, so the overlap is a closed select box sitting above the
  button for as long as it takes to choose, and gone afterwards.

  scrollIntoView is still attempted first, on the chance the drawer can scroll:
  it uses the browser's own scrolling and works on nested scrollers where a
  scrollTop assignment does not. It is a bonus, not the mechanism.

  ================================================================
  3. THE DEAD SCROLL AT THE BOTTOM, AND THE WHITE SPACE UNDER CHECKOUT

  Two measured faults, one cause each.

  THE FREEZE: the drawer's scrolling element reports scrollHeight 1392 against
  clientHeight 844 -- 548px of content it cannot reach, because assigning
  scrollTop to it does nothing (it reads back 0). With overscroll-behavior at
  its default of `auto`, dragging past that dead end CHAINS the gesture to the
  page behind the drawer, and iOS spends a beat rubber-banding the wrong
  element before it will accept an upward drag again. That is the "pane freezes
  and won't let you scroll back up for a second or two". `contain` keeps the
  gesture inside the drawer, so the dead end stops rather than bounces.

  THE WHITE SPACE UNDER CHECKOUT. Two wrong guesses came first, and both are
  worth recording so they are not tried a fourth time:

    - bottom:-34px is NOT the cause. Forcing it to 0 measured WORSE: the pane's
      bottom edge moved from y=844 (flush) to y=810, opening a real 34px gap.
      That negative offset cancels the drawer's own 34px bottom padding.
    - The layout is not broken in Chrome at all. Measured at viewport heights
      620, 660, 900 and 1000 with one item, the pane's bottom sat exactly on the
      viewport bottom every time -- gap 0. Chasing it in a desktop browser was
      never going to find it.

  WHAT IT ACTUALLY IS. The drawer (.m6pn) is position:fixed with height:100%.
  On iOS Safari that resolves against the LAYOUT viewport -- the full screen,
  including the strip behind the browser's own toolbar -- while what the shopper
  sees is the VISUAL viewport, which is shorter whenever the toolbar (and, in a
  theme preview, the Shopify bar) is showing. So the drawer is taller than the
  visible area, its bottom edge is off-screen behind those bars, and the last
  thing actually visible above them is white drawer with nothing in it.

  Two changes close it, and they work together:

    - The drawer's height is set from window.visualViewport.height, and kept in
      step as that changes (the toolbar collapsing on scroll fires resize). The
      drawer then ends exactly where the visible area ends. In Chrome
      visualViewport.height equals innerHeight, so nothing moves there -- which
      is why this is safe to ship without regressing the desktop that already
      measured correct.
    - .sticky-in-panel gets margin-top:auto. .m6pn is already a flex column, so
      this pins the pane to the BOTTOM of that column whenever the content is
      shorter than the drawer, instead of leaving it stranded mid-way with white
      underneath. It is inert when the content overflows, which is the case the
      sticky positioning already handled.

  The result is CHECKOUT sitting on the bottom edge of what the shopper can see,
  which is what was asked for.

  ================================================================
  4. THE FREE-SHIPPING BAR MATCHES THE WORDMARK BOX ABOVE IT

  Measured, the two boxes in .nc-drawer-top disagreed on every dimension:

      .pg-cart-mark   x=32  w=329  radius 12px   padding 11px 10px 9px   #0B0710
      .nc-dship       x=55  w=284  radius 100px  padding 7px 20px        transparent

  -- a full-width dark rounded-rectangle with a narrower transparent pill
  floating under it. The shipping bar now takes the same width (a block with the
  same margins, so it tracks the wordmark box at any drawer width rather than
  being pinned to 329px), the same 12px corners, the same padding and the same
  fill, with its text and icon lightened to sit on that fill. Both breakpoints.

  ================================================================
  5. STARS EITHER SIDE OF THE WORDMARK

  Three small stars each side of POCKETERA, injected rather than written into
  the markup because .nc-drawer-top is rendered by pg-drawer and rebuilt on every
  cart change; they are re-applied on each rebuild and are aria-hidden, so the
  drawer still announces the shop name once.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* --- 3. see note above --- */
  /* .m6pn is a SIBLING of #cart, not a descendant -- measured: a `#cart .m6pn`
     rule matched nothing. Listed bare, and #cart kept for the drawer itself. */
  #cart,
  .m6pn,
  #cart .l4ca{
    overscroll-behavior:contain;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;
  }
  /* --- 3. the pane sits at the bottom of the drawer column -- see note above --- */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel{margin-top:auto}

  /* --- 2. an OPEN chooser paints above the pinned pane -- see note above.
     Only while .is-open, so nothing overlaps CHECKOUT in the normal state. --- */
  #cart .pg-unlock.is-open{position:relative;z-index:6}
  #cart .pg-unlock.is-open .pg-unlock-pick{position:relative;z-index:6}

  /* --- 4. the free-shipping bar wears the wordmark box's shape --- */
  #cart .nc-dship,
  .nc-drawer-top .nc-dship{
    display:flex !important;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    gap:8px;
    width:auto !important;
    margin:0 0 8px !important;
    padding:11px 10px 9px !important;
    border-radius:12px !important;
    background:#0B0710 !important;
    color:#E4D9F0 !important;
  }
  #cart .nc-dship svg,
  .nc-drawer-top .nc-dship svg{stroke:#C79BEA !important}

  /* --- 5. the stars --- */
  #cart .pg-cart-star,
  .nc-drawer-top .pg-cart-star{
    color:#C79BEA;
    opacity:.75;
    font-size:10px;
    letter-spacing:.22em;
    vertical-align:middle;
    pointer-events:none;
  }
  #cart .pg-cart-star.pg-cs-l,
  .nc-drawer-top .pg-cart-star.pg-cs-l{margin-right:9px}
  #cart .pg-cart-star.pg-cs-r,
  .nc-drawer-top .pg-cart-star.pg-cs-r{margin-left:9px}

  @media (max-width:760px){
    /* make the picture read as tappable: a pointer, a suppressed grey iOS tap
       flash (the row supplies its own feedback below), and no long-press image
       callout, which otherwise offers "Save Image" instead of following it */
    #cart .l4ca li figure{
      cursor:pointer;
      -webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;
      -webkit-touch-callout:none;
    }
    #cart .l4ca li figure img{pointer-events:none}
    /* a brief press state so the tap is acknowledged even before the page moves */
    #cart .l4ca li figure:active{opacity:.72;transition:opacity .06s ease}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgCartImgLink) return; window.pgCartImgLink = 1;

  /* Products whose picture is NOT a link. Matched on a handle FRAGMENT so the
     rule survives the handle being renamed around it (the case's handle carries
     a "-free-gift" suffix today). Both of the case's variants -- the free one
     and the paid spare -- share this handle, so both are covered. */
  var SKIP = ['r36s-protective-case'];

  function excluded(href){
    for (var i = 0; i < SKIP.length; i++){
      if (href.indexOf(SKIP[i]) > -1) return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  /* The row's own product link is the source of truth for where the picture
     should go: it is what the theme itself rendered for this line, so the
     picture can never point somewhere the row does not. */
  function hrefFor(li){
    var a = li.querySelector('a[href*="/products/"]');
    return a ? a.getAttribute('href') : '';
  }

  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if (e.button !== 0 || e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.altKey) return;
    if (!window.matchMedia('(max-width:760px)').matches) return;

    var fig = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('#cart .l4ca li figure');
    if (!fig) return;

    /* never take a tap that belongs to a control that was already there */
    if (e.target.closest('a, button, input, select, textarea, label, [role="button"]')) return;

    /* a tap that ends a text selection is not a tap on the picture */
    var sel = window.getSelection && window.getSelection();
    if (sel && sel.type === 'Range' && String(sel).length) return;

    var li = fig.closest('li');
    if (!li) return;

    var href = hrefFor(li);
    if (!href || excluded(href)) return;

    e.preventDefault();
    window.location.href = href;
  }, true);

  /* ---- 2. bring the free-orb chooser out from behind the pinned pane ---- */
  function scroller(){
    var el = document.querySelector('#cart .l4ca');
    while (el && el !== document.body){
      var s = getComputedStyle(el);
      if (/auto|scroll/.test(s.overflowY) && el.scrollHeight > el.clientHeight + 4) return el;
      el = el.parentElement;
    }
    return document.querySelector('#cart .m6pn') || document.querySelector('.m6pn');
  }

  function reveal(){
    try {
      var pick = document.querySelector('#cart .pg-unlock.is-open .pg-unlock-pick');
      if (!pick) return;
      var pane = document.querySelector('#cart .sticky-in-panel');
      if (!pane) return;
      var pk = pick.getBoundingClientRect();
      var pn = pane.getBoundingClientRect();
      var over = pk.bottom - pn.top;          /* how far the picker runs under the pane */
      if (over <= 0) return;                  /* already clear: never jump for nothing */

      /* the z-index rule above has already made it visible; this only tries to
         bring it fully into view as well. scrollIntoView first because it works
         on nested scrollers that ignore a scrollTop assignment -- which this one
         does. Both are best-effort: neither is what makes the picker usable. */
      try { pick.scrollIntoView({block: 'center', behavior: 'smooth'}); } catch(e2){}
      var sc = scroller();
      if (sc) sc.scrollTop += over + 14;
    } catch(e){ /* a failed scroll must never break the cart */ }
  }

  /* ---- 3. the drawer ends where the shopper's screen ends ----
     see the note above: height:100% on a fixed element is the LAYOUT viewport on
     iOS, which is taller than what is visible whenever the browser toolbar is
     up. visualViewport reports the visible box, so the drawer is sized from it
     and kept in step. Guarded on the API existing, and a no-op in browsers where
     the two are already equal. */
  function fitDrawer(){
    try {
      var vv = window.visualViewport;
      if (!vv) return;
      var aside = document.querySelector('.m6pn');
      if (!aside) return;
      if (!window.matchMedia('(max-width:760px)').matches){
        aside.style.removeProperty('height');
        aside.removeAttribute('data-pg-h');
        return;
      }
      var h = Math.round(vv.height);
      if (aside.getAttribute('data-pg-h') === String(h)) return;   /* settle */
      aside.setAttribute('data-pg-h', String(h));
      aside.style.setProperty('height', h + 'px', 'important');
    } catch(e){}
  }
  fitDrawer();
  if (window.visualViewport){
    window.visualViewport.addEventListener('resize', fitDrawer);
    window.visualViewport.addEventListener('scroll', fitDrawer);
  }
  window.addEventListener('resize', fitDrawer);
  window.addEventListener('orientationchange', function(){ setTimeout(fitDrawer, 250); });

  /* ---- 5. stars either side of the wordmark ---- */
  function stars(){
    try {
      var mark = document.querySelector('.nc-drawer-top .pg-cart-mark');
      if (!mark) return;
      if (mark.querySelector('.pg-cart-star')) return;     /* already dressed */
      var word = mark.querySelector('.pg-wordmark');
      if (!word) return;
      var l = document.createElement('span');
      l.className = 'pg-cart-star pg-cs-l';
      l.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
      l.textContent = '\u2726\u2726\u2726';
      var r = l.cloneNode(true);
      r.className = 'pg-cart-star pg-cs-r';
      mark.insertBefore(l, word);
      if (word.nextSibling) mark.insertBefore(r, word.nextSibling);
      else mark.appendChild(r);
    } catch(e){}
  }
  stars();

  /* the drawer is rebuilt wholesale on every cart change, which throws both of
     the above away -- re-apply on each rebuild */
  if (window.MutationObserver){
    var drawerEl = document.getElementById('cart') || document.querySelector('.m6pn');
    if (drawerEl){
      var q = false;
      new MutationObserver(function(){
        if (q) return;
        q = true;
        setTimeout(function(){ q = false; fitDrawer(); stars(); }, 120);
      }).observe(drawerEl, {childList: true, subtree: true});
    }
  }
  [400, 1200, 2600].forEach(function(t){ setTimeout(function(){ fitDrawer(); stars(); }, t); });

  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if (!e.target.closest) return;
    if (!e.target.closest('.pg-unlock-add')) return;
    /* the panel is built after a fetch, so look once it can exist, then again
       in case the drawer re-rendered under it */
    setTimeout(reveal, 260);
    setTimeout(reveal, 900);
  }, true);
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Imglink", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Cart Imglink"}]}
{% endschema %}
